Z||000000||CRAGAR||10-22-1999||07:58 AM||||Has anyone purchased and installed the aluminum battery box sold by West Coast Fiero's?  It's used to relocate the battery to the front underneath the spare tire.  I'd like to hear about your experience with it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||JIM GOOSE||10-22-1999||10:49 AM||||  I relocated my battery using a plastic boat box which I mounted on the passenger side of the front compartment. I just removed the tire & now carry one of those inflator in a can deals. You could put the spare in the trunk if you wanted to carry it. I think that I  can visualize their setup, probably cut an opening in the tire well & stick the box into it. You could do this with a boat box & fab some brackets.  I bought my components separately & paid less than for a kit, did fab my own brackets & weld them.  Bought 20' of 2ga cable, terminals & fabed the pos. cable to the starter. If you need more info, you can contact me at <A HREF="http://www.hamptonmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.hamptonmotorsports.com</A>    JMSG||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||10-22-1999||10:50 AM||||I have them in steel. Contact me for info.||||reg||1
